# No environment variables are needed.
#
# This site is entirely static: plain HTML, CSS and JS plus recipes.json.
# There is no backend, no database and no third-party API, so nothing here
# should ever hold a value. The file exists so that anyone cloning the repo
# can see at a glance that there is nothing to configure.
#
# If you later add something that does need a key (a form endpoint, an
# analytics service), add it below with an EMPTY value and set the real value
# in the Netlify dashboard under Site configuration → Environment variables.
#
# FORM_ENDPOINT=
